desc:TwoStorms IR Loader
tags: convolution impulse response cabinet IR loader
author: TwoStorms
version: 1.0

// An impulse-response loader with an Act built in: its output gain, meters, Auto (Target, Match, Reference),
// Drive link and Finale are a TwoStorms Act, so TwoStorms Gain Stage lists and stages it like one.
// Two IRs, blended: each with on, level, pan, delay (to a hundredth of a millisecond), phase, stereo width, high and
// low pass (12, 24 or 48 dB/oct) and solo. With two: their starts lined up, IR 2's timing and polarity matched to IR 1
// (cross-correlation) and its loudness matched (A-weighted). Tail trim at a level, stereo IRs (left and right) or
// summed, stereo or mono input (mono IRs on a mono input: one real convolution, about half the CPU), dry/wet.
// Drop .wav files on the window, browse anywhere (with the helper script), or step through an IR's folder; the IRs
// are saved with the project. True zero latency (a direct head and partitioned FFT convolution), or 64, 128 or 256
// samples of latency for less CPU. Changes crossfade.
// Hold-to-hear level-matched Bypass. Needs REAPER 6.74 or newer.

slider1:0<0,3,1{2,4,6,8}>-Channels
slider2:0<0,2,1{Auto,Always,Never}>-Finale (Auto = the last Act in the chain)
